From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:47:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(movement): keep sprint boost in the Java attribute
 modifier

The local player's Bedrock movement value already includes sprint, but
translation sends it as a Java base with no modifiers. A client mod that
reapplies setSprinting(true) then adds Java's boost to that boosted base,
raising the attribute from 0.13 to 0.169.

Send the clamped effective speed divided by the sprint multiplier as the
base, together with Java's minecraft:sprinting modifier and its exact
float-promoted amount. Repeated sprint calls replace that modifier by id.
Keep Bedrock attribute state, server overrides, other native modifiers,
and native limits intact; normalize only the local player's Java output.

Packet regression tests cover repeated sprint calls, start/stop, server
speed updates, other native modifiers, zero speed, and both native limits.
A local probe against Minecraft 26.3 attribute operations reproduces the
reported double boost. CubeCraft gameplay speed remains unmeasured.
